n prose dark:prose-invert w-full wrap-break-word light markdown-new-styling=
"><p data-start=3D"0" data-end=3D"114">What you=E2=80=99re seeing is <stron=
g data-start=3D"22" data-end=3D"51">actually correct behavior</strong>, and=
 it happens for a specific reason. Let me explain clearly.</p>
<h2 data-section-id=3D"1eo03m1" data-start=3D"116" data-end=3D"157">Why you=
 still see long unreadable text</h2>
<p data-start=3D"158" data-end=3D"293">The image you uploaded <strong data-=
start=3D"181" data-end=3D"205">contains hidden bits</strong>, but those bit=
s <strong data-start=3D"222" data-end=3D"292">do not contain a properly enc=
oded message with a stop marker (<code data-start=3D"286" data-end=3D"289">=
#</code>)</strong>.</p>
<p data-start=3D"295" data-end=3D"504">Your extractor reads <strong data-st=
art=3D"316" data-end=3D"345">LSB bits from every pixel</strong>, so it keep=
s converting them to characters. Because dataset stego images usually hide =
<strong data-start=3D"432" data-end=3D"468">compressed or encrypted payload=
s</strong>, the output becomes something like:</p>
<pre class=3D"overflow-visible! px-0!" data-start=3D"506" data-end=3D"523">=
<div class=3D"relative w-full mt-4 mb-1"><div class=3D""><div class=3D"rela=
